        "@value": true
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "If a masonry wall has a vulnerability that is ‘excessive slenderness’ and a vulnerability that is ‘absence of top curbstone’ and a vulnerability that is ‘presence of horizontal thrusts’ and a behaviour that is ‘inadequate out of plane behaviour’, then it has an occurring mechanism that is ‘horizontal bending’."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "Horizontal bending - absence of top curbstone"
      }
    ],
